('minor-asc-african-american-and-african-studies', 'minor', 'African American and African Studies Minor', 'College of Arts and Sciences', 'Arts and Sciences minor advising sheets (2026)', 15, 2.0, '15 credit hours. Required courses, groups and caps are on the official advising sheet: https://artsandsciences.osu.edu/sites/default/files/2023-05/minor-aaas.pdf 12-18 credit hours at the 2000 level or above, at least 6 upper-division; C- or better in each course and a 2.00 GPA across the minor; no Pass/Non-Pass, at most 3 hours of X193 and 3 of S/U; up to 6 hours of transfer/exam credit; up to two courses may overlap the GE (one if the minor has fewer than four courses). The minor must be in a different subject than the major and have 12 hours that don''t overlap the major or other minors. Declare it at least one term before graduating.', 'https://artsandsciences.osu.edu/sites/default/files/2023-05/minor-aaas.pdf', 500, array['asc-aaas-ba']::text[], null, null, null, null, '{}'::text[], '{}'::jsonb),
